| Field                 | Type   | Always Present | Description |
|-----------------------|--------|----------------|-------------|
| variable              | string | No             | Name of another global variable referenced in the template |
| host_list             | array  | No             | Static host list |
| dynamic_group_list    | array  | No             | Dynamic group list |
| topo_node_list        | array  | No             | CMDB topology node list |
| container_list        | array  | No             | Static container list |
| container_filter_list | array  | No             | Container filter list |

##### host_list[] element

| Field       | Type   | Always Present | Description |
|-------------|--------|----------------|-------------|
| bk_host_id  | long   | No             | Host ID in CMDB |
| bk_cloud_id | long   | No             | Cloud area ID |
| ip          | string | No             | Host IP address |

##### dynamic_group_list[] element

| Field | Type   | Always Present | Description |
|-------|--------|----------------|-------------|
| id    | string | Yes            | Dynamic group ID |

##### topo_node_list[] element

| Field      | Type   | Always Present | Description |
|------------|--------|----------------|-------------|
| id         | long   | Yes            | Topology node ID |
| node_type  | string | Yes            | Topology node type. Allowed values: `module`, `set` |

##### container_list[] element

| Field         | Type   | Always Present | Description |
|---------------|--------|----------------|-------------|
| container_id  | long   | Yes            | Container ID (CMDB internal ID) |
| container_uid | string | No             | Container runtime UID |
| name          | string | No             | Container name |
| pod_name      | string | No             | Pod name |
| namespace     | string | No             | Namespace name |
| cluster_uid   | string | No             | Cluster UID |
| node_ip       | string | No             | IP of the node hosting the container |

Fields other than `container_id` come from the snapshot taken at save time and are meant for display. Containers
saved through other entries (such as the OpenAPI write APIs) may carry only `container_id`. Once a container is
deleted from CMDB, what was saved is still returned here.

##### container_filter_list[] element

| Field           | Type   | Always Present | Description |
|-----------------|--------|----------------|-------------|
| name            | string | No             | Filter name |
| kube_topo_list  | array  | Yes            | Topology path list |
| prop_conditions | array  | No             | Container property conditions |

###### kube_topo_list[] element

| Field         | Type   | Always Present | Description |
|---------------|--------|----------------|-------------|
| cluster       | object | Yes            | Cluster topology object, e.g. `{"id": 105}` |
| namespace     | object | No             | Namespace topology object, e.g. `{"id": 207}` |
| workload_list | array  | No             | Workload topology objects, e.g. `{"kind": "deployment", "id": 309}` |

Topology objects carry CMDB internal IDs only, without readable information such as cluster UID or namespace name.

###### prop_conditions[] element

| Field | Type   | Always Present | Description |
|-------|--------|----------------|-------------|
| field | string | Yes            | Field to filter on. Allowed values: `container_name`, `container_container_uid`, `pod_name`, `pod_labels` |
| value | string | Yes            | Value. A Kubernetes label selector expression when `field` is `pod_labels` |

No operator is returned: the match type is determined solely by the field. The values match what the web console
uses, so the response can be written back to the write APIs as is.
